            "<p>Direct Taxes</p>",
            "<p>Income tax, corporate tax</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Indirect Taxes</p>",
            "<p>GST, customs duty, excise duty</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c3tjc90",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Goods and Services Tax (GST)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nd8v4qf",
      "content": "• Introduced on 1 July 2017"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "oc2111x",
      "content": "• Replaced many indirect taxes"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6999w9i",
      "content": "• Known as 'One Nation One Tax' reform"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "00dmurp",
      "content": "• Types: CGST, SGST and IGST"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The word 'Budget' is nowhere mentioned in the Constitution of India; Article 112 uses the term 'Annual Financial Statement'.",
        "Differentiate clearly between Revenue Deficit, Fiscal Deficit, and Primary Deficit for conceptual MCQs.",
        "GST is a destination-based, comprehensive indirect tax levied on the supply of goods and services."
      ],
      "id": "7oomlr5"
    },
    {
      "id": "zrsukvl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Budget Deficit"
    },
    {
      "id": "g1zqdln",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Deficit Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Meaning</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Fiscal Deficit</p>",
            "<p>Total expenditure minus total revenue</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Revenue Deficit</p>",
            "<p>Revenue expenditure minus revenue receipts</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Primary Deficit</p>",
            "<p>Fiscal deficit minus interest payments</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "njbysxc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ioh3n0y",
      "content": "• Union Budget is presented by the Finance Minister."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "87r6j7r",
      "content": "• Financial year in India is April to March."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7fzxncl",
      "content": "• GST was implemented in India in 2017."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i6hnssl",
      "content": "• Article 112 of the Constitution deals with the Union Budget."
    }
  ],
